---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---
<SiteLayout
  title="Needs Attention for Jira — Bomray Lab"
  description="Documentation for Needs Attention for Jira by Bomray Lab."
>
  <main>
    <section class="container app-hero">
      <div class="app-hero-grid">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Jira Cloud App</span>
          <h1>Needs Attention for Jira</h1>
          <p>Review Jira projects, custom fields, filters, and dashboards that may require administrator attention. See clear evidence before deciding what to do.</p>
          <div class="badge-row">
            <span class="badge">Built with Atlassian Forge</span>
            <span class="badge">No automatic cleanup</span>
            <span class="badge">English & Korean</span>
          </div>
          <div class="actions">
            <a
              class="button primary"
              href="https://marketplace.atlassian.com/apps/3107345287/needs-attention-for-jira"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              data-ga-event="marketplace_cta_click"
              data-ga-location="apps_hero"
            >View on Marketplace</a>
            <a class="button" href="#getting-started">Get started</a>
            <a class="button" href="/support/">Contact support</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <img class="app-icon-large" src="/assets/logo.png" alt="Needs Attention for Jira icon">
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="container docs-layout">
        <aside class="docs-nav" aria-label="Documentation navigation">
          <strong>Documentation</strong>
          <a href="#overview">Overview</a>
          <a href="#features">Features</a>
          <a href="#getting-started">Getting started</a>
          <a href="#workflow">Review workflow</a>
          <a href="#history">Scan history</a>
          <a href="#snooze">Snooze</a>
          <a href="#security">Data & security</a>
          <a href="#faq">FAQ</a>
        </aside>

        <div>
          <section class="docs-section" id="overview">
            <h2>Overview</h2>
            <p>Needs Attention for Jira gives Jira Cloud administrators a focused review workspace. It identifies configuration items that may need attention and explains why each item was flagged.</p>
            <div class="note">The app does not automatically delete, archive, or modify Jira resources. Administrators remain in control of every decision.</div>
          </section>

          <section class="docs-section" id="features">
            <h2>Features</h2>
            <div class="feature-grid">
              <div class="feature">
                <strong>Overview dashboard</strong>
                <p>See health score, priority breakdowns, and top review items.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="feature">
                <strong>Project review</strong>
                <p>Review stale, inactive, empty, or poorly owned projects.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="feature">
                <strong>Custom field review</strong>
                <p>Inspect usage, context, screens, and scope before making changes.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="feature">
                <strong>Filter and dashboard review</strong>
                <p>Find items that may no longer be useful, shared, favorited, or clearly owned.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="feature">
                <strong>Scan history</strong>
                <p>Track changes across saved scan snapshots.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="feature">
                <strong>Snapshot comparison</strong>
                <p>Identify new, resolved, changed, and unchanged items.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="feature">
                <strong>Snooze workflow</strong>
                <p>Temporarily hide an item for 30, 60, or 90 days.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="feature">
                <strong>Configurable rules</strong>
                <p>Adjust thresholds and preferences for your Jira environment.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="docs-section" id="getting-started">
            <h2>Getting started</h2>
            <ol class="step-list">
              <li>Install <strong>Needs Attention for Jira</strong> from the <a href="https://marketplace.atlassian.com/apps/3107345287/needs-attention-for-jira" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-ga-event="marketplace_cta_click" data-ga-location="apps_getting_started">Atlassian Marketplace</a>.</li>
              <li>Open <strong>Apps &gt; Needs Attention</strong> in Jira.</li>
              <li>From the <strong>Overview</strong> page, click <strong>Run Scan</strong> to analyze your Jira configuration.</li>
              <li>Select a resource type such as <strong>Projects</strong>, <strong>Custom Fields</strong>, <strong>Filters</strong>, or <strong>Dashboards</strong>.</li>
              <li>Review the evidence and details for each item before taking action.</li>
            </ol>
            <p class="note">The initial scan may take longer depending on the size of your Jira site.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="docs-section" id="workflow">
            <h2>Review workflow</h2>
            <h3>1. Start from Overview</h3>
            <p>Overview summarizes Projects, Custom Fields, Filters, and Dashboards that need review.</p>
            <h3>2. Open a review category</h3>
            <p>Each category provides a prioritized list.</p>
            <h3>3. Inspect evidence</h3>
            <p>Evidence explains why the item was flagged. Details provide additional Jira context.</p>
            <h3>4. Continue in Jira</h3>
            <p>Use the action button to open the related Jira configuration page. The app does not make the change for you.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="docs-section" id="history">
            <h2>Scan history</h2>
            <p>Each manual scan creates a snapshot of the current review result.</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>New:</strong> newly detected</li>
              <li><strong>Resolved:</strong> no longer detected</li>
              <li><strong>Changed:</strong> evidence or priority changed</li>
              <li><strong>Unchanged:</strong> remains the same</li>
            </ul>
          </section>

          <section class="docs-section" id="snooze">
            <h2>Snooze</h2>
            <p>Snooze temporarily removes an item from the active review list for 30, 60, or 90 days. Changes are reflected after the next scan.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="docs-section" id="security">
            <h2>Data and security</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>Built on Atlassian Forge</li>
              <li>No external Bomray Lab application server</li>
              <li>No automatic deletion or configuration modification</li>
              <li>History and preferences use Atlassian-hosted Forge storage</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Read the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for details.</p>
          </section>

          <section class="docs-section" id="faq">
            <h2>FAQ</h2>
            <h3>Does the app automatically delete or archive anything?</h3>
            <p>No. It only identifies items for review and provides supporting evidence.</p>
            <h3>When does Jira data get scanned?</h3>
            <p>A fresh scan runs when an administrator selects <strong>Run Scan</strong>.</p>
            <h3>Can I change the review criteria?</h3>
            <p>Yes. Available thresholds and preferences can be managed from Settings.</p>
            <h3>How do I get help?</h3>
            <p>Visit <a href="/support/">Support</a> or email <a href="mailto:support@bomraylab.com">support@bomraylab.com</a>.</p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
